From 679ad03acb55dd19f54df2df3862b45f1ecf4e8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:34:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Newton solver: line search by backtracking on the norm of the
 residual
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Option LineSearch of the Newton solver (None by default, Backtracking):
the step of an iteration is halved until the norm of the residual
decreases sufficiently, ||r(x - θ c)|| <= [1 - t θ (1 - η)] ||r(x)||, the
inexact Newton backtracking of Eisenstat and Walker (t = 1e-4, η being the
adapted tolerance of the linear solve, ten reductions at most). An estimate
at which the integration of the behaviours fails is a refused trial, the
reductions are not counted as iterations, and the resolution fails if no
step is acceptable (accepted as convergence below the
StagnationRelativeTolerance). An accepted full step requires no other
integration nor residual than the ones of the next iteration.

The settings, the reading of the options and the search are in the
LineSearch structure, on the model of AdaptiveLinearSolverTolerance. With
the first choice of Eisenstat and Walker, the tolerance which follows a
reduced step uses the norm of the linear model at this step,
||(1 - θ) r - θ (J c - r)||, given by the norms of r and of J c - r and by
their scalar product (setLinearResidual, setStepLength): one scalar product
per iteration, no product by the operator.

Without the option, the iterations are unchanged: the code of the
correction, of its reduction on an integration failure and of the adaptive
tolerance is the same.

Tests: LineSearchTest (options, criterion and failures on scalar
equations), AdaptiveLinearSolverToleranceTest (norm of the linear model
compared to the one computed on vectors) and NewtonLineSearchTest, with the
test behaviour SaturatingElasticity (non linear elasticity whose stress
saturates): a cube loaded close to the saturation then unloaded in one time
step, for which the Newton solver oscillates without line search and
converges to the analytical solution with it; integration failures refused
by the search; plastic cube; stagnation.
